this used to be his home and a shop that  provided him income now all that Anna  Salman has left is rubble his house  collapsed after flash floods hit his  town of lje in Sudan's Khartoum state on  Monday the water destroyed most of their  belongings this shop was the only means  I had to support myself and my family in  the house was the only place we had to  live all of that is gone now and there's  nothing I can do but say it's God's will  the floods have destroyed at least 700  houses here according to the town's  Disaster Response Committee leaving more  than 300 families displaced Sudanese  authorities say rains and flash floods  in the past two weeks have destroyed  over 12,000 homes across the country  most of the damage is in poor  neighborhoods with shoddy drainage  infrastructure basic services have also  been affected life has become hard there  is no electricity the water lines have  been affected there are no shops working  no bakeries working everything has  become hard more rain and a rise in  river water levels are expected in the  coming days adding to concerns of more  floods to come but that's not all flash  floods have not only destroyed homes  here in El Jani  they've also turned roads like this one  into rivers and because it can take days  sometimes weeks for them to dry out it's  feared stagnant waters will bring  diseases over the past few years health  workers have recorded an increase in the  number of malaria and cholera fatalities  due to stagnant waters during rainy  seasons affected residents blamed the  former government out stood in April of  neglect  now opposition leaders say steps need to  be taken to ensure that what happened in  Angelli  doesn't happen again because we only you  know having this registration in place  we need some deeds we need to build new  dams new barriers located so as to  prevent floods coming from the far east  of a gayly it is more than having  legislation in place it is about  political will  it is about restructuring the area  coming  new ideas to prevent any floods in the  future for Ernest who has to pick up the  pieces to rebuild his home starting over  won't be easy and with the rainy season  not yet over  he hopes no more flash floods come to  take away what little he has left  Hiba Morgan al Jazeera Horton
 

